Unofficial LineageOS 23.0 for Samsung Galaxy Tab A 10.5 (2018) WiFi
===========

How to build
---------------
- Follow the official LineageOS wiki for setting up the build environment up to the *Initialize the LineageOS source repository* section: https://wiki.lineageos.org/devices/husky/build/

- Clone LineageOS sources:

```
    repo init -u https://github.com/UDPSendToFailed/android.git -b lineage-23.0 --git-lfs
    repo sync
```

- Create folders for the device-specific sources and clone them:

```
    mkdir -p device/samsung/gta2xlwifi
    git clone https://github.com/UDPSendToFailed/android_device_samsung_gta2xlwifi.git -b lineage-23.0 device/samsung/gta2xlwifi/
    
    mkdir -p kernel/samsung/gta2xlwifi
    git clone https://github.com/UDPSendToFailed/android_kernel_samsung_gta2xlwifi.git -b lineage-23.0 kernel/samsung/gta2xlwifi/
    
    mkdir -p vendor/samsung
    git clone https://github.com/UDPSendToFailed/proprietary_vendor_samsung.git -b lineage-23.0 vendor/samsung/
```

- Download and set up ARM's GNU toolchain:

```
    cd ~/android
    mkdir gcc14 && cd gcc14

    wget https://developer.arm.com/-/media/Files/downloads/gnu/14.3.rel1/binrel/arm-gnu-toolchain-14.3.rel1-x86_64-aarch64-none-linux-gnu.tar.xz
    wget https://developer.arm.com/-/media/Files/downloads/gnu/14.3.rel1/binrel/arm-gnu-toolchain-14.3.rel1-x86_64-arm-none-linux-gnueabihf.tar.xz

    tar -xf arm-gnu-toolchain-14.3.rel1-x86_64-aarch64-none-linux-gnu.tar.xz
    tar -xf arm-gnu-toolchain-14.3.rel1-x86_64-arm-none-linux-gnueabihf.tar.xz

    rm -r ~/android/lineage/prebuilts/gcc/linux-x86/aarch64/aarch64-linux-android-4.9/bin
    rm -r ~/android/lineage/prebuilts/gcc/linux-x86/arm/arm-linux-androideabi-4.9/bin

    cp -r ~/android/gcc14/arm-gnu-toolchain-14.3.rel1-x86_64-aarch64-none-linux-gnu/* ~/android/lineage/prebuilts/gcc/linux-x86/aarch64/aarch64-linux-android-4.9/
    cp -r ~/android/gcc14/arm-gnu-toolchain-14.3.rel1-x86_64-arm-none-linux-gnueabihf/* ~/android/lineage/prebuilts/gcc/linux-x86/arm/arm-linux-androideabi-4.9/

    cd ~/android/lineage/prebuilts/gcc/linux-x86/aarch64/aarch64-linux-android-4.9/bin && for f in aarch64-none-linux-gnu-*; do mv "$f" "${f/none-linux-gnu/linux-android}"; done
    cd ~/android/lineage/prebuilts/gcc/linux-x86/arm/arm-linux-androideabi-4.9/bin && for f in arm-none-linux-gnueabihf-*; do mv "$f" "${f/none-linux-gnueabihf/linux-androideabi}"; done

    cd ~/android/lineage/prebuilts/gcc/linux-x86/aarch64/aarch64-linux-android-4.9/bin && ln -s aarch64-linux-android-gcc aarch64-linux-android-gcc-4.9 && ln -s aarch64-linux-android-gcc aarch64-linux-androidkernel-gcc
    cd ~/android/lineage/prebuilts/gcc/linux-x86/arm/arm-linux-androideabi-4.9/bin && ln -s arm-linux-androideabi-gcc arm-linux-androideabi-gcc-4.9 && ln -s arm-linux-androideabi-gcc arm-linux-androidkernel-gcc

    rm -r ~/android/gcc14
```

- Build the ROM:

```
    cd ~/android/lineage
    . build/envsetup.sh
    brunch lineage_gta2xlwifi-bp2a-userdebug
```

If everything goes as expected, the resulting TWRP flashable zip should be in `out/target/product/gta2xlwifi/`.
